 @TheBitKrieger  The full 12Gb runs on a 192bit bus at full speed. There would only be a thin bus if it had 8Gb or any other number other than 6Gb or 12Gb.

GDDR6 memory is available in 1Gb and 2Gb chips, each with a 32bit bus. Six chips with a 32bit bus add up to 192bit. Whether 1Gb or 2Gb chips are used, it still adds up to 192 when six are used.

The 6Gb version of the 3060 will be released at a later date.

